h4. Blacklists

Three different things hide posts here, and only one of them is yours to change.

h4. Your blacklist

A list of tags, one rule per line, in your settings. A post matching a rule is hidden from listings; click it to see it anyway. Tags on one line are ANDed, and "-" excludes:

[code]
rating:e
arthropod rating:e -pokemon_(creature)
[/code]

A new account starts with the site's default blacklist and can change it freely.

[b]One limit:[/b] your blacklist cannot match a tag you are not allowed to see. Some creators keep their tags private; those tags are not in the page at all for you, so no rule can catch them. The alternative would be telling you what they were.

h4. The enforced blacklist

Applied to every viewer, stored in no account, and editable by nobody from the site. It hides certain combinations the same way your blacklist does -- hidden, not removed, and still reachable by direct link.

h4. Banished tags

Some tags have been removed from the site's vocabulary outright. They do not appear in listings, in autocomplete, or on posts, for anyone. This is about the words; posts that carried them are dealt with separately. Admins can reveal them for themselves with a setting, and only for themselves.

These are separate from gated content, which is about what a post [i]is[/i] rather than what you have chosen to hide. See [[help:censored_tags]].
